  "stem": "The mass, in grams, of algae growing in a laboratory tank \\(d\\) days after the start of an experiment is modeled by \\(M(d) = 20(2)^{\\frac{d}{5}}\\). According to the model, how many days after the start of the experiment will the mass of the algae be 160 grams?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "15"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Set \\(20(2)^{\\frac{d}{5}} = 160\\) and divide by \\(20\\): \\(2^{\\frac{d}{5}} = 8\\).",
    "\\(8 = 2^{3}\\), so \\(\\frac{d}{5} = 3\\).",
    "Therefore \\(d = 15\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "d = symbols('d')\nsol = solve(Eq(20*2**(d/5), 160), d)\nassert sol == [15]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == sol",
